The {{nihongo|'''Hitotsubashi Line'''|一橋線|Hitotsubashi-sen}} is a subway line in [[Okami|Okami (大紙)]], [[Okaiken]], operated by [[Okami Metro]]. It serves as a strategic northern feeder line, connecting the dense residential districts of [[Higashiyodogawa Ward, Okami|Higashiyodogawa]] with the major northern terminal of [[Umeda-Kita Station|Umeda-Kita]]. On system maps, the line is color-coded crimson red ({{Okami Metro color|H}}), and its stations use the prefix "H".

Designated as Line 12, the Hitotsubashi Line is the final line in the Okami Metro network. Unlike the standard third-rail subway lines, it utilizes overhead catenary electrification (1,500 V DC). This design choice was made to facilitate seamless reciprocal through-service with the [[Akitetsu|Akitetsu (Akita Railway)]], allowing commuters from the northern prefecture of [[Akita Prefecture|Akita]] to travel directly into Okami's northern business district without transferring.



==History==
Originally planned as the "Kita Extension" in the 1990s, the project was rebranded as the Hitotsubashi Line (named after the historic bridge located near the northern terminus) to distinguish it from the wider "Kita" district.

Construction began in 2000 to alleviate the heavy congestion on the parallel [[Miyoshi Line]]. The entire 8.9&nbsp;km route opened on December 24, 2006. It immediately became a vital artery for the northern suburbs, providing a direct link to the [[Akitetsu]] network which serves the inter-regional commuters from the north.

