==Rolling Stock==
The Hitotsubashi Line requires trains capable of handling overhead electrification (1,500 V DC) to match the Akitetsu network.

* [[Okami Metro 9000 series|9000 series]] (6-car sets):
*: The exclusive Okami Metro fleet for Line 12. Introduced in 2006, these trains feature a stainless steel body with a **crimson red** band. They are equipped with heavy-duty snow plows and enhanced climate control to handle the colder winters when running through-services into the northern mountains of Akita Prefecture.
* [[Akitetsu]] 3000 series (6-car sets):
*: Private railway stock owned by Akitetsu. These trains are famous for their "Classic Maroon" livery, plush velvet seating, and wood-grain interiors, offering a premium commuting experience.

